<title>GERMANY: AUDI SAYS H1 PRE-TAX PROFIT UP 20.9 PCT.</title>
<headline>AUDI SAYS H1 PRE-TAX PROFIT UP 20.9 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>INGOLSTAT, Germany 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     489     vs up 20.9 pct</p>
<p>    Group sales				  10,600  vs up 13.7 pct</p>
<p>    Group deliveries (units)		 276,052 vs up 12.6 pct</p>
<p>    Group German deliveries		  121,835 vs up 10.5 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carmaker is Audi AG. The company is a unit of Volkswagen AG. The company also said it increased its share of the German market to 6.8 percent from 5.8 percent at the same time a year ago.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom + 49 228 260 97150</p>
</text>
